IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cor-dates`
IMPORT `cor-core`

-- Coroners Act 2003 (SA) -- THE SEAT OF THE FAMILY MEMBER: the relative of a person who has died or disappeared in
-- South Australia, who meets the coronial process and may later bring or answer a claim about the death. Some groups
-- are for the same person in another situation the Act puts them in: as the one who must report a death, as a witness
-- at the inquest, or as someone whose interests or competence a finding touches. Every question is asked as that person
-- would ask it, from facts that person can state; the State Coroner's, the Court's and the Supreme Court's opinions are
-- asked as conditions ("the Court is of the opinion ..."). The rules are in cor-core.l4; this module restates none.
--
-- Based on content from the South Australian Legislation website (version of 31 January 2023, fetched 6 November
-- 2026). CC BY 4.0. BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `The family member's questions`

§§ `Is the death one the coroner deals with (ss 3, 21)`
-- Situation: a member of your family has died, or has disappeared.

@export Is my family member's death a "reportable death" that the State Coroner must be told about (Coroners Act 2003 (SA) s 3(1), (2), (2a))?
GIVEN `died in SA` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the death happened in South Australia (including its coastal sea and the airspace above it)
      `place unknown but possibly SA` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the place of death is unknown but it is reasonably possible that it was in South Australia
      `body in SA` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the body is in South Australia
      `cause in SA` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a cause of the death happened, or possibly happened, in South Australia
      `lived in SA` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether they were ordinarily resident in South Australia when they died
      `travelling to SA` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether they died on an aircraft or vessel whose flight or voyage was to a place of disembarkation in South Australia
      `unexpected or unnatural` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the death was by an unexpected, unnatural, unusual, violent or unknown cause
      `in flight or on a voyage` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether they died on an aircraft during a flight or on a vessel during a voyage
      `custody` IS A `Custody situation` @desc Where they were when the death, or its cause or a possible cause, happened or may have happened: not detained or held; detained in a South Australian place under an Act or law (including home detention); absent from detention without an escort; being apprehended or held by someone authorised under South Australian law; being apprehended or held in South Australia under another jurisdiction's law; being apprehended or held outside South Australia only under another jurisdiction's law; evading apprehension; escaping or trying to escape
      `order` IS AN `Order situation` @desc Whether they died of natural causes, as certified by a doctor, while under a Mental Health Act 2009 inpatient treatment order (in a ward wholly, or not wholly, set aside for mental illness) or a Guardianship and Administration Act 1993 s 32(1)(b) order; otherwise none
      `procedure within 24 hours` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether they died during, as a result of, or within 24 hours of a surgical procedure, an invasive medical or diagnostic procedure, or an anaesthetic given for one
      `procedure excluded` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that procedure is one the regulations say this does not apply to
      `died outside hospital` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether they died somewhere other than a hospital
      `discharged within 24 hours` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether they died within 24 hours of being discharged from a hospital after being an inpatient
      `emergency within 24 hours` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether they died within 24 hours of seeking emergency treatment at a hospital
      `protected or in care` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether at death they were a protected person under the Aged and Infirm Persons' Property Act 1940 or the Guardianship and Administration Act 1993, a child in the custody or guardianship of the Minister or Chief Executive under the Children and Young People (Safety) Act 2017, a patient in an approved treatment centre under a Mental Health Act, a resident of a licensed supported residential facility, or accommodated for drug addiction treatment
      `consented treatment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether they died during, as a result of, or within 24 hours of medical treatment consented to under Part 5 of the Guardianship and Administration Act 1993 or Part 2A of the Consent to Medical Treatment and Palliative Care Act 1995
      `no death certificate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether no certificate as to the cause of death has been given to the Registrar of Births, Deaths and Marriages
      `prescribed circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the death happened in circumstances the regulations prescribe
      `died outside SA` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether they died outside South Australia
      `authorisation elsewhere` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a coroner of another State or Territory has authorised the release or disposal of the body under that place's Coroners Act
      `voluntary assisted dying` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the death resulted from a voluntary assisted dying substance administered under the Voluntary Assisted Dying Act 2021
GIVETH A `Reportable answer`
`Is my family member's death a reportable death` MEANS
    `is it a reportable death (s 3)` (`Death facts` WITH
        `state death` IS `is a State death (s 3(1))` `died in SA` `place unknown but possibly SA` `body in SA` `cause in SA` `lived in SA` `travelling to SA`
        `unexpected, unnatural, unusual, violent or unknown cause` IS `unexpected or unnatural`
        `on an aircraft in flight or a vessel on a voyage` IS `in flight or on a voyage`
        `in custody` IS `is a death in custody (s 3(1), s 21(4))` `custody` `order`
        `during, as a result of, or within 24 hours of a surgical, invasive medical or diagnostic procedure or its anaesthetic` IS `procedure within 24 hours`
        `the procedure is one the regulations exclude` IS `procedure excluded`
        `died outside a hospital` IS `died outside hospital`
        `within 24 hours of discharge after being an inpatient` IS `discharged within 24 hours`
        `within 24 hours of seeking emergency treatment at a hospital` IS `emergency within 24 hours`
        `a protected or supervised person at death` IS `protected or in care`
        `during, as a result of, or within 24 hours of treatment consented to under the guardianship or consent laws` IS `consented treatment`
        `no cause of death certificate given to the Registrar` IS `no death certificate`
        `circumstances prescribed by the regulations` IS `prescribed circumstances`
        `died outside SA` IS `died outside SA`
        `a corresponding authorisation was issued elsewhere` IS `authorisation elsewhere`
        `voluntary assisted dying substance under the 2021 Act` IS `voluntary assisted dying`)

@export Was my family member's death a "death in custody" (Coroners Act 2003 (SA) s 3(1), s 21(4))?
GIVEN `custody` IS A `Custody situation` @desc Where they were when the death, or its cause or a possible cause, happened or may have happened (see the choices)
      `order` IS AN `Order situation` @desc Whether they died of certified natural causes under a mental health inpatient treatment order or a guardianship detention order, and in what kind of ward
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Was it a death in custody` MEANS `is a death in custody (s 3(1), s 21(4))` `custody` `order`

@export Must there be an inquest into my family member's death, disappearance, or the fire or accident (Coroners Act 2003 (SA) s 21(1), (4), (5))?
GIVEN `event` IS AN `Event` @desc What happened: a death; the disappearance from anywhere of a South Australian resident; the disappearance of anyone from or within South Australia; a fire or accident causing injury to a person or property; an event another Act requires an inquest into; or another event
      `custody` IS A `Custody situation` @desc For a death: where they were when the death, or its cause, happened or may have happened
      `order` IS AN `Order situation` @desc For a death: whether they died of certified natural causes under a mental health inpatient order or a guardianship detention order, and in what kind of ward
      `reportable or would be but for interstate release` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a death: whether it is a reportable death, or would be one except that they died outside South Australia and a coroner elsewhere authorised the body's release
      `State Coroner or Attorney-General wants one` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the State Coroner considers an inquest necessary or desirable, or the Attorney-General has directed one
GIVETH AN `Inquest answer`
`Must there be an inquest` MEANS
    `must an inquest be held (s 21(1))` `event` (`is a death in custody for s 21(1)(a)` `custody` `order`) `reportable or would be but for interstate release` (`is a s 21(5) natural causes case` `order`) `State Coroner or Attorney-General wants one`

@export Someone has been charged with causing the death or event: can the inquest go ahead (Coroners Act 2003 (SA) s 21(2))?
GIVEN `someone charged` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a person has been charged in criminal proceedings with causing the event the inquest is about
      `criminal proceedings over` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether those criminal proceedings have been disposed of, withdrawn or permanently stayed
GIVETH A `Criminal charge answer`
`Does a criminal charge hold up the inquest` MEANS `does a criminal charge hold up the inquest (s 21(2))` `someone charged` `criminal proceedings over`

§§ `Who speaks for the family (ss 20A, 29, 37A)`

@export Am I my family member's "senior next of kin" (Coroners Act 2003 (SA) ss 20A(5), 29(3), 37A(9))?
GIVEN `my relationship` IS A `Relationship` @desc How you were related to the person: their spouse (legally married) or domestic partner, the most recent if there was more than one; an earlier spouse or partner; an adult child (18 or over); a parent (or guardian, if they were a child); an adult brother or sister; a person named as executor in their will; their legal personal representative; or someone else
      `available spouse or partner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether they had a spouse or domestic partner (the most recent) who is available
      `available adult child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether they have an adult child who is available
      `available parent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether they have a living parent who is available
      `available adult sibling` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether they have an adult brother or sister who is available
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Am I the senior next of kin` MEANS `is a senior next of kin` `my relationship` `available spouse or partner` `available adult child` `available parent` `available adult sibling`

@export Am I "family" of the person, for the family's lawyer at an inquest and for the release of records (Coroners Act 2003 (SA) ss 20A(5), 37A(9))?
GIVEN `senior next of kin` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are the person's senior next of kin
      `descendant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person was a descendant of the indigenous inhabitants of Australia or the Torres Strait Islands
      `identified` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person regarded themself as Aboriginal or Torres Strait Islander (or, if a child, was so regarded by at least one parent)
      `kinship` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are held to be related to the person according to Aboriginal or Torres Strait Islander kinship rules
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Am I family` MEANS `is family (ss 20A(5), 37A(9))` `senior next of kin` (`is an Aboriginal or Torres Strait Islander person (s 20A(5))` `descendant` `identified`) `kinship`

§§ `At the inquest (ss 19, 20, 20A, 23, 23A)`
-- Situation: an inquest is being held.

@export Can I attend the inquest (Coroners Act 2003 (SA) s 19)?
GIVEN `clearing order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Court has ordered the court cleared, or evidence suppressed, under Part 8 of the Evidence Act 1929 or in the interests of national security
GIVETH AN `Open court answer`
`Can I attend the inquest` MEANS `is the inquest open to the public (s 19)` `clearing order`

@export Am I entitled to appear at the inquest, personally or through a lawyer, and question witnesses (Coroners Act 2003 (SA) s 20(1), (2))?
GIVEN `Court finds my interest sufficient` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Court is of the opinion that you have a sufficient interest in the subject or result of the proceedings
GIVETH AN `Appearance answer`
`Can I appear at the inquest` MEANS `may I appear (s 20)` `Court finds my interest sufficient`

@export Can our family's lawyer appear at the inquest as of right and question witnesses (Coroners Act 2003 (SA) s 20A)?
GIVEN `about a death or disappearance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the inquest is about the death or disappearance of a person
      `lawyer engaged by the family` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the lawyer is a legal practitioner engaged by or on behalf of the family to represent them in these proceedings
      `lawyer nominated by the family` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the family has nominated the lawyer as its nominated representative in accordance with the Court's rules
GIVETH A `Family representative answer`
`Can our family's lawyer appear` MEANS `may the family's lawyer appear (s 20A)` `about a death or disappearance` `lawyer engaged by the family` `lawyer nominated by the family`

@export Must I answer this question, or produce this document, at the inquest (Coroners Act 2003 (SA) ss 23(5), 23A(1)-(4))?
GIVEN `privileged` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether answering or producing it would breach legal professional privilege
      `I object` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you object because the answer or document may tend to incriminate you, or make you liable to a penalty, under an Australian or foreign law
      `Court finds reasonable grounds` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Court has determined that there are reasonable grounds for your objection
      `foreign law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the answer may tend to incriminate you, or expose you to a penalty, under the law of a foreign country
      `Court finds justice requires it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Court is satisfied that the interests of justice require you to answer
GIVETH AN `Answering answer`
`Must I answer this question at the inquest` MEANS `must I answer (ss 23(5), 23A)` `privileged` `I object` `Court finds reasonable grounds` `foreign law` `Court finds justice requires it`

@export Will I be given a certificate protecting my answer at the inquest (Coroners Act 2003 (SA) s 23A(5), (6))?
GIVEN `how I answered` IS A `How the answer was given` @desc What happened: whether you objected on self-incrimination or penalty grounds, whether the Court found reasonable grounds (then or afterwards), and whether you answered willingly or because the Court required you to
GIVETH A `Certificate answer`
`Will I get a certificate` MEANS `will I be given a certificate (s 23A(5), (6))` `how I answered`

@export Can what I said at the inquest be used against me in later proceedings, such as a damages claim or a prosecution (Coroners Act 2003 (SA) s 23A(8)-(10))?
GIVEN `I have a certificate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Court gave you a certificate under s 23A for the answer or document
      `prosecuted for a false answer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the later proceeding is a criminal proceeding about the falsity of that answer or document
GIVETH A `Use answer`
`Can my inquest answer be used against me` MEANS `can the answer be used against me (s 23A(8)-(10))` `I have a certificate` `prosecuted for a false answer`

§§ `The findings and what follows (ss 25, 26, 27)`
-- Situation: the inquest has finished, or is about to.

@export Can the inquest decide this, for example who is liable to pay damages for the death (Coroners Act 2003 (SA) s 25(1)-(3))?
GIVEN `what I want found` IS A `Finding sought` @desc What you want the Court to find: the cause and circumstances; a recommendation; that someone is civilly liable (must pay damages or compensation); or that someone is criminally liable
GIVETH A `Finding answer`
`Can the inquest find this` MEANS `can the inquest find it (s 25(1)-(3))` `what I want found`

@export Will I be sent a copy of the inquest findings and recommendations (Coroners Act 2003 (SA) s 25(4))?
GIVEN `death in custody inquest` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the inquest was into a death in custody
      `I appeared` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you appeared at the inquest, personally or by a lawyer
      `Court finds my interest sufficient` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Court is of the opinion that you have a sufficient interest in the matter
GIVETH A `Copy of findings answer`
`Will I be sent the findings` MEANS `will I be sent the findings (s 25(4))` `death in custody inquest` `I appeared` `Court finds my interest sufficient`

@export When does the Minister's 6 months to respond to an inquest recommendation end? The Minister must report to Parliament within 8 sitting days after that day (Coroners Act 2003 (SA) s 25(5)).
GIVEN `Minister received it on` IS A DATE @desc The day the Minister received a copy of the recommendation (ISO 8601, e.g. 2025-03-15)
GIVETH A DATE
`When do the Minister's 6 months end` MEANS `the day the Minister's 6 months end (s 25(5))` `Minister received it on`

@export Can the inquest be re-opened (Coroners Act 2003 (SA) s 26)?
GIVEN `Attorney-General directs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Attorney-General has directed the State Coroner to re-open the inquest
GIVETH A `Re-opening answer`
`Can the inquest be re-opened` MEANS `can the inquest be re-opened (s 26)` `Attorney-General directs`

@export Can I appeal to the Supreme Court against an inquest finding (Coroners Act 2003 (SA) s 27(1), (7))?
GIVEN `affects my money` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the finding affects, or may affect, your pecuniary (financial) interests, for example your exposure to a claim
      `reflects on my competence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the finding reflects adversely on your competence in your trade, profession or occupation
      `Supreme Court finds another interest` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Supreme Court is of the opinion that you have some other interest sufficient to ground an appeal
GIVETH A `Sufficient interest answer`
`Can I appeal against the finding` MEANS `may I appeal against the finding (s 27(1), (7))` `affects my money` `reflects on my competence` `Supreme Court finds another interest`

@export By when must I appeal against an inquest finding: the last day of the month after the findings are given (Coroners Act 2003 (SA) s 27(3))?
GIVEN `findings given on` IS A DATE @desc The day the Coroner's Court gave its findings (ISO 8601, e.g. 2025-03-15)
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must I appeal` MEANS `the last day to appeal (s 27(3))` `findings given on`

@export Is my appeal against an inquest finding in time (Coroners Act 2003 (SA) s 27(3), (4))?
GIVEN `findings given on` IS A DATE @desc The day the Coroner's Court gave its findings
      `appealed on` IS A DATE @desc The day you applied (or will apply) to the Supreme Court
      `time extended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Supreme Court has extended the time for your appeal
GIVETH AN `Appeal time answer`
`Is my appeal in time` MEANS `is my appeal in time (s 27(3), (4))` `findings given on` `appealed on` `time extended`

§§ `Reporting a death (s 28)`
-- Situation: you know of a death that may be one the coroner deals with.

@export Must I report this death, and to whom (Coroners Act 2003 (SA) s 28(1), (2)(a))?
GIVEN `may be reportable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the death you know of is, or may be, a reportable death (unexpected or unnatural, after a procedure, in custody, and so on)
      `in custody` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is a death in custody
      `believe already reported` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you believe on reasonable grounds that it has already been reported, or that the State Coroner otherwise knows of it
GIVETH A `Reporting answer`
`Must I report this death` MEANS `must I report the death (s 28)` `may be reportable` `in custody` `believe already reported`

@export When I report a death, must I also give my opinion as to its cause (Coroners Act 2003 (SA) s 28(2)(b))?
GIVEN `I am notifying` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are the person notifying the State Coroner or police of the death
      `I am a doctor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a medical practitioner
      `I cared for or examined them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were responsible for the person's medical care before death, or examined the body after death
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Must I give my opinion on the cause` MEANS `must I give my opinion on the cause (s 28(2)(b))` `I am notifying` `I am a doctor` `I cared for or examined them`

@export What is the largest fine for this offence under the Coroners Act 2003 (SA) (ss 20(6), 22(5), 28, 34, 36)? 0 means the offence carries imprisonment only.
GIVEN `offence` IS AN `Offence` @desc The offence: not reporting a reportable death; not giving information or a medical opinion when notifying; a knowingly false written statement in evidence; obstructing a person exercising a coroner's power; divulging information; or contempt of the Coroner's Court
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is the largest fine` MEANS `the maximum fine in dollars` `offence`

@export What is the longest prison term, in years, for this offence under the Coroners Act 2003 (SA) (ss 20(6), 22(5), 28, 34, 36)? 0 means no imprisonment.
GIVEN `offence` IS AN `Offence` @desc The offence (as for the fine question)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is the longest prison term` MEANS `the maximum imprisonment in years` `offence`

§§ `The body and the cause of death (ss 22, 29, 32)`
-- Situation: the death is with the State Coroner.

@export Can my family member's body be released to us for the funeral (Coroners Act 2003 (SA) s 32)?
GIVEN `reportable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the death is a reportable death
      `body in SA` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the body is in South Australia
      `authorisation issued` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the State Coroner has issued an authorisation for the disposal of human remains for the body
      `dispute` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the State Coroner knows of a dispute about who is entitled at law to possession of the body for its burial or cremation
GIVETH A `Body answer`
`Can the body be released to us` MEANS `can the body be released (s 32)` `reportable` `body in SA` `authorisation issued` `dispute`

@export Can the coroner order a post-mortem, the removal of the body, or an exhumation (Coroners Act 2003 (SA) s 22(1)(g)-(i), (2))?
GIVEN `step` IS A `Body step` @desc What is to be done: a post-mortem examination; removing the body to a specified place; or exhuming the body or retrieving the ashes
      `who` IS A `Who acts` @desc Who is acting: the State Coroner (deciding whether to hold an inquest) or the Coroner's Court (for an inquest)
      `Attorney-General approves` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For an exhumation by the State Coroner: whether the Attorney-General has approved it
GIVETH A `Body step answer`
`Can the coroner do this to the body` MEANS `can it be done to the body (s 22)` `step` `who` `Attorney-General approves`

@export Who will make the finding as to the cause of my family member's death, and can it be closed as "undetermined natural causes" (Coroners Act 2003 (SA) s 29)?
GIVEN `notified reportable death` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the State Coroner has been notified of the death as a reportable death
      `inquest held or required` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an inquest is being held, or is required (a death in custody, or one the State Coroner or Attorney-General wants)
      `State Coroner believes natural causes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the State Coroner, after obtaining medical information or advice, has reasonable grounds to believe the death was due to natural causes
      `senior next of kin consented` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a senior next of kin has consented in writing, as the State Coroner or the regulations require, to no further investigation, inquiry or inquest into the precise cause
GIVETH A `Cause finding answer`
`Who finds the cause of death` MEANS `who finds the cause of death (s 29)` `notified reportable death` `inquest held or required` `State Coroner believes natural causes` `senior next of kin consented`

§§ `Records and information (ss 34, 37, 37A)`

@export Can I see, or get a copy of, this inquest material (Coroners Act 2003 (SA) s 37)?
GIVEN `material` IS AN `Inquest material` @desc What you want: process forming part of the Court's records; a transcript of evidence; documentary material admitted into evidence; a transcript of the findings and recommendations; an order of the Court; or other material
      `not in open court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it was not taken or received in open court
      `suppressed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Court suppressed it from publication
      `photo or recording` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is a photograph, slide, film, video or audio tape, or other recording of images or sound
      `prescribed class` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is of a class the regulations prescribe as needing permission
GIVETH AN `Access answer`
`Can I see the inquest material` MEANS `can I see or copy it (s 37)` `material` `not in open court` `suppressed` `photo or recording` `prescribed class`

@export From what day can our family apply for the coroner's records where no inquest was held (Coroners Act 2003 (SA) s 37A(2))?
GIVEN `finding or decision on` IS A DATE @desc For a reportable death, the day of the finding as to the cause of death (or of undetermined natural causes); for any other event, the day the State Coroner decided not to hold an inquest
GIVETH A DATE
`From when can our family apply for the records` MEANS `the first day the family may apply (s 37A(2))` `finding or decision on`

@export Must the State Coroner give our family the records about the death or event, where no inquest was held (Coroners Act 2003 (SA) s 37A)?
GIVEN `no inquest decided` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the State Coroner decided that no inquest would be held into the death or event
      `I am family` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are the person's family (senior next of kin, or for an Aboriginal or Torres Strait Islander person, a relative under kinship rules)
      `finding or decision on` IS A DATE @desc For a reportable death, the day of the finding as to cause; otherwise, the day of the decision not to hold an inquest
      `applying on` IS A DATE @desc The day you apply
      `not in the interests of justice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the State Coroner is satisfied that it is not in the interests of justice to provide the records
GIVETH A `Family records answer`
`Must the State Coroner give us the records` MEANS `must the State Coroner give the family the records (s 37A)` `no inquest decided` `I am family` `finding or decision on` `applying on` `not in the interests of justice`

@export May I pass on information about a person that I obtained through the coronial process (Coroners Act 2003 (SA) s 34)?
GIVEN `publicly known` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the information is publicly known
      `law requires or allows it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether this Act or another Act or law requires or authorises you to divulge it (for example a subpoena or court order)
      `needed to administer an Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is reasonably required in connection with the administration of this Act or another Act
      `for proceedings arising from the coronial process` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is for legal proceedings arising out of the administration of this Act (such as an appeal against a finding)
      `to a government agency` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are giving it to a government agency or instrumentality of South Australia, the Commonwealth or another State or Territory for its proper functions
      `the person consents` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person the information is about consents
GIVETH A `Divulging answer`
`May I pass on the information` MEANS `may I divulge the information (s 34)` `publicly known` `law requires or allows it` `needed to administer an Act` `for proceedings arising from the coronial process` `to a government agency` `the person consents`

§§ `Claims against the coronial system (ss 33, 35)`

@export Can I hold the coroner, the Court's staff or an investigator liable for what they did in the coronial process (Coroners Act 2003 (SA) s 33)?
GIVEN `who` IS AN `Official` @desc Who you want to hold liable: a coroner; or a member of the Court's staff, an investigator (including a police officer) or a person assisting an investigator
      `honest` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether their act or omission was honest
      `in official functions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it was done in carrying out, or purportedly carrying out, their official functions
GIVETH AN `Immunity answer`
`Can I hold them liable` MEANS `can I hold them liable (s 33)` `who` `honest` `in official functions`

@export Can I call the coroner as a witness in my claim or other case (Coroners Act 2003 (SA) s 35)?
GIVEN `about coronial work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the evidence is about something that came to the coroner's knowledge in the administration of the Act
      `coroner prosecuted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the proceedings are against the coroner for an offence
GIVETH A `Coroner witness answer`
`Can I call the coroner as a witness` MEANS `can I call the coroner as a witness (s 35)` `about coronial work` `coroner prosecuted`
